[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 968,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 733,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139679,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 288,
        "headingId": 733,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Orbital chondroma is a benign chondrocytic neoplasm, producing hyaline or myxoid cartilage, and arising periosteally or in orbital soft tissue.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 969,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 734,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139680,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 288,
        "headingId": 734,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9220/0 Chondroma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 970,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 735,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139681,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 288,
        "headingId": 735,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E89.1 &amp; XH0NS4 Benign tumours of uncertain differentiation, soft tissue &amp; Chondroma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 971,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 736,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139682,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 288,
        "headingId": 736,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> chondroma of soft parts; extraskeletal chondroma; periosteal chondroma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended</em>: juxtacortical chondroma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 972,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 737,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139683,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 288,
        "headingId": 737,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 973,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 738,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139684,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 288,
        "headingId": 738,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Orbital chondromas arise in the superomedial orbit in the vicinity of the trochlea, which is the only cartilaginous structure found normally in the orbit {5981161;26265654;17117112;17446102;1578865}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 974,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 739,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139685,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 288,
        "headingId": 739,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours are solitary and present as a painless firm mass in the superomedial orbit. Ptosis and restrictive strabismus have been reported {17446102;17117112;26265654}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 975,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 740,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139686,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 288,
        "headingId": 740,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Orbital chondroma is extremely rare, accounting for 1&nbsp;of 645&nbsp;orbital masses in one survey {6497741}. Of 3&nbsp;reported cases in the English-language literature, all included male patients, aged 9&ndash;27&nbsp;years {26265654;17117112;17446102}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 976,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 741,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139687,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 288,
        "headingId": 741,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 977,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 742,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139688,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 288,
        "headingId": 742,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Genetic analysis of orbital chondroma has not been performed. Location in the region of the trochlea suggests an origin from residual chondroid progenitor cells in this area.</p>\r\n<p>Cytogenetic analyses of limited numbers of soft tissue chondromas of other sites reveal variable aberrations, including rearrangements of 12q13-q15 and trisomy&nbsp;5. In a set of tumours with rearrangements of 12q13-q15, a truncated or full-length <em>HMGA2</em> transcript was found {8402563;10748295;11793371;14614053;25250651}. In about 50% of the cases, <em>FN1</em> gene rearrangements were reported, with <em>FGFR1</em> and <em>FGFR2</em> as fusion partners {31273315}. Periosteal chondromas may harbour mutations in <em>IDH1</em> {21598255}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 984,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 749,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139689,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 288,
        "headingId": 749,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Orbital chondroma is a 10&ndash;20&nbsp;mm, well-circumscribed, nodular, solid greyish-bluish-white mass. Myxoid/cystic change may be present.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 978,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 743,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139690,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 288,
        "headingId": 743,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour is composed of lobules of well-formed hyaline and/or myxoid cartilage delineated by fibrous septa. Chondrocytes are arranged in clusters and reside within lacunar spaces or float in a flocculent myxoid matrix. The nuclei are usually small, round, and dark, but may be enlarged with fine or coarse chromatin and small nucleoli, and exhibit mild pleomorphism. Coarse calcifications and endochondral ossification may be present {17446102}. Mitotic activity is absent or very low and abnormal mitotic figures are not observed. If periosteal, there should be no invasion of the underlying cortex.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 979,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 744,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139691,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 288,
        "headingId": 744,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 980,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 745,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139692,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 288,
        "headingId": 745,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 983,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 748,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139693,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 288,
        "headingId": 748,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> soft tissue mass composed of well-delineated cartilage nodules; matrix is hyaline or myxoid and may calcify; chondrocytes show limited atypia and no or little mitotic activity.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 981,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 746,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139694,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 288,
        "headingId": 746,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 982,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 747,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139695,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 288,
        "headingId": 747,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Marginal excision is curative. Recurrence has not been reported, although experience is limited.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]